    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Silla grew from Saro, a chiefdom at Gyeongju traditionally founded in 57 BCE, into one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#korea">Korea</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms</a>.</li><li>Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>, it destroyed Baekje in 660 and Goguryeo in 668, then expelled Tang forces by 676.</li><li>Its bone-rank aristocracy presided over a Buddhist golden age that produced Bulguksa and the Seokguram grotto.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>King Munmu, who completed Silla's unification, is said to have asked for burial at sea so that he could become a dragon guarding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#korea">Korea</a>; a rock islet off the coast near Gyeongju is held to be his tomb.</p></aside>
    </section>

